n if I go off on a riff about one thing or another, he's able to pull it back into a different place, right? If it needs to be and vice versa. So here's what I would say. I enjoy doing all this stuff. I guess maybe I'm a ham. I don't know. I was on air in TV news for a number of years. So I enjoyed the performance aspect of it, but I also enjoy the friendship aspect of it. Because, for example, just last night, Brent and I were on the phone talking over what the next episodes are going to be. Well, that's just fun. I mean, it's work, but it's fun. And that's the thing you look for in a good performance. You want your work to look like it's not so onerous.

