so the CIA has been involved with Hollywood over the years in ways that we don't even quite understand completely. Because first, it's secret. And second of all, the CIA is very good. They don't put things in records. They don't write it down so you can go get a Freedom of Information Act about it. In fact, the thing about the CIA has always been, what's the quote? The quote is, nothing in writing, right? If you've got a secret, don't put it in writing. So yeah, that's kind of how we look at this thing. It was the moment that charged us up on this topic. And you might say, well, why in the world would you wait 30 years to talk about it? Well, we've sort of talked about it a little bit over time, but we were busy with other careers and so forth. And there are other reasons. But at a certain point in your life or your career, you go, hey, if I'm going to tell this story, I better do it now. I'm not the young guy I used to be. So I'm like, hey, if we're going to talk about this, Brent, let's not wait another year or two. Let's just get this thing over with. So season one of Sound, Light and Frequency is all about that. And by the way, I just point this out. If you're saying, well, how do I even watch this thing? It's pretty simple. Go wherever you listen to podcasts, type in Sound, Light, Frequency. Pretty much you'll find the show. And we have a website, soundlightfrequency.com. Although the show itself is called, just for the record, Sound, Light, and Frequency. And if you want to know why the show is called that, that is, that falls into spoiler territory. You got to watch episode one to find out why we would ever name a podcast Sound, Light, and Frequency.

