<v SPEAKER_2>Yeah, absolutely. And the last thing I will add is that, for anyone that is interested in the series, understand that we have 36 episodes to tell several decades worth of personal stories. But we're using each episode kind of, we're taking a movie or a TV show or sometimes in certain episodes, multiple ones, as portals into a certain aspect of ufology, right? And then using that as a springboard to tell some of our personal stories. And so I think the expectation is, you know, we set certain things in motion in the first episode, bringing JC up, introducing this idea of the formula that he gave us. And did we take the deal? What is the formula? All of those things will be answered over the next 36 episodes. We are trying to tell the story in the same way to a certain effect, the way we experienced it, right? We didn't have all the answers up front, right? And so we want to take people on the same kind of ride that we did, where it's like we had to struggle and fight and make sense of different things. And we're going to try and replicate that experience to some degree in the course of our storytelling. But rest assured, everything that we know by the end of 36 episodes will be out on the table, and it'll be open to interpretation, and we will have our own theories, but we can't wait to hear everyone's theories as well.

